# DRY (always on)

Read and follow `.cursor/skills/dry-refactoring/SKILL.md` when cleaning duplication.

## Rules

- Before writing new helpers, search the repo for an existing one (especially money, dates, expense status, API fetch).
- If you paste the same block twice in one change, extract it in that same change.
- Prefer one shared function over parallel copies that will drift (e.g. bill drawer hosted from Suppliers vs Bills page).
- Do not invent layers “for reuse later” — extract when a second real call site exists (pairs with Ponytail).
- Meaningful clones: run `npx jscpd --reporters ai <path>` then apply the dry-refactoring workflow (highest line-count first).

## This codebase hotspots

Money formatting, expense status pills, daily-entry line drafts, and ledger bill/pay drawers have already forked once — extend the shared path instead of adding a third copy.
